# Choice Hierarchy

User choices form a hierarchy where higher levels inform lower-level defaults.

## Levels

ChoiceLevels {
  L1_Lifecycle => PoC | Throwaway | TeamTool | MVP | EarlyProduction | MatureProduction | Legacy
  L2_Params => Risk, Team, Velocity, Scale
  L3_Ecosystem => language/runtime
  L4_Stack => Framework, StateManagement, Database, TestRunner, Deployment, CICD
  L5_Libraries => specific packages within stack
}

## Rules

CascadeRules {
  Higher informs lower => Lifecycle shapes reasonable defaults
  Explicit overrides inferred => user choice beats cascade
  Record both => store explicit AND inferred separately
}

## Inference Chains

L2FromL1 {
  PoC | Throwaway => (Personal, Solo, Rapid, Local)
  TeamTool => (Internal, Small, Active, Team)
  MVP => (Business, Small, Active, Users)
  EarlyProduction => (Business, Multiple, Active, Users)
  MatureProduction => (Business+, Multiple, Measured, Organization)
}

## Output Structure

choices.mdc => source of truth (L1-L5 with explicit/inferred markers)
core.mdc => derived from L1 + L2
stack/*.mdc => derived from L3-L5, calibrated to L1 + L2
